WEBVTT

00:03.644 --> 00:05.355
I miss you, too,
but what are you doing up?

00:05.356 --> 00:08.407
Isn't it, like, 3:00
in the morning in London?

00:08.409 --> 00:10.876
Yeah, I've been having trouble
sleeping, too.

00:10.878 --> 00:15.697
Alan suggested warm milk
and masturbation,

00:15.699 --> 00:19.218
but that's his answer
for pretty much everything.

00:19.220 --> 00:20.753
No, don't worry.

00:20.755 --> 00:22.671
He's not gonna live here
forever.

00:22.673 --> 00:25.591
More importantly, uh,
when are you coming back?

00:25.593 --> 00:29.711
Ugh! Really, another week?

00:29.713 --> 00:31.313
All right, that settles it.

00:31.315 --> 00:33.682
I'm gonna heat up some milk.

00:33.684 --> 00:36.218
Okay, all right.

00:36.220 --> 00:38.053
Try to get some sleep.

00:38.055 --> 00:39.655
I love you.

00:39.657 --> 00:43.225
No, I love &lt;i>you&lt;/i> more.

00:43.227 --> 00:45.361
No, uh-uh, I love you more.

00:45.363 --> 00:46.529
(makes kissing
sounds)

00:46.531 --> 00:47.830
(Jake laughs)

00:47.832 --> 00:50.399
(making
kissing sounds)

00:50.401 --> 00:52.251
You got a problem with love?

00:52.253 --> 00:54.403
Uh-uh.
No, no.

00:56.089 --> 00:57.706
Sorry.

00:57.708 --> 00:59.241
Oh, it's Jake and his friend.

00:59.243 --> 01:02.744
No, he's not gonna stay here
forever, either.

01:04.548 --> 01:06.515
All right, bye-bye.
Sweet dreams.

01:06.517 --> 01:09.769
Sorry, we'll get out
of your way.

01:09.771 --> 01:11.020
Nah, that's okay.

01:11.022 --> 01:12.772
What are you guys doing?

01:12.774 --> 01:14.774
Well, we were gonna
play a video game

01:14.776 --> 01:16.942
on the big screen,
but if you're busy...

01:16.944 --> 01:17.893
No, no, come on.

01:17.895 --> 01:20.079
Nice.
Awesome.

01:20.081 --> 01:21.113
Where's your dad?

01:21.115 --> 01:22.898
Oh, he's out with
this guy's mom.

01:22.900 --> 01:24.400
Yeah, they're picking
my grandma up

01:24.402 --> 01:26.368
at the International House
of Old People.

01:28.155 --> 01:30.772
I-Hoop.

01:30.774 --> 01:32.774
She's in a rest home?

01:32.776 --> 01:34.943
I guess
they're resting.

01:34.945 --> 01:37.296
They don't move
very much.

01:37.298 --> 01:38.714
Oh, except on pudding day.

01:38.716 --> 01:40.916
Uh, then you could
get trampled.

01:40.918 --> 01:44.136
Wow. Your dad's meeting
his girlfriend's mother.

01:44.138 --> 01:45.805
That's a big step.

01:45.807 --> 01:47.640
What's bigger than
boning each other?

01:47.642 --> 01:48.654
Shut up!

01:48.679 --> 01:50.424
Come on. We both
know they're doing it.

01:50.561 --> 01:52.428
- We've heard them.
- Dude!

01:52.430 --> 01:55.231
Oh, Alan!
Oh, Lyndsey!

01:55.233 --> 01:57.566
Okay, quit it,
or I'm leaving.

01:57.568 --> 01:58.767
Okay, fine.

01:58.769 --> 01:59.935
And I'm taking my game.

01:59.937 --> 02:01.604
I apologize.
Accepted.

02:01.606 --> 02:04.607
It's nice you guys have a sense
of humor about that stuff.

02:04.609 --> 02:07.660
So many kids of divorce are,
like, so angry all the time.

02:07.662 --> 02:09.695
Yeah, well, it's kind of
hard to stay angry

02:09.697 --> 02:11.697
when you smoke
as much pot as we do.

02:11.699 --> 02:13.833
Truth.

02:13.835 --> 02:18.370
When my dad left, I was, like,
really angry.

02:18.372 --> 02:19.505
What did you do?

02:19.507 --> 02:20.756
Just channeled my energy

02:20.758 --> 02:22.291
into learning how
to program computers.

02:22.293 --> 02:24.844
Made my first million
by the time I was 20.

02:24.846 --> 02:27.179
- Oh, that's our plan, too.
- Totally.

02:27.181 --> 02:29.498
Really? What language
do you guys code in?

02:29.500 --> 02:31.350
Java? Perl? C-Plus-Plus?

02:31.352 --> 02:33.519
Um...

02:33.521 --> 02:36.605
Okay, maybe not a million.

02:36.607 --> 02:38.891
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men,
men, men ♪

02:38.893 --> 02:40.632
♪ Ah.
♪ Men.

02:40.633 --> 02:44.533
&lt;font color="#00FF00">♪ Two and a Half Men 9x19 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00FFFF">Palmdale, Ech&lt;/font>
