02:50.129 --> 02:51.628
You're in a good mood.

02:51.630 --> 02:52.796
I am.

02:52.798 --> 02:54.481
Looking forward to
seeing your mother?

02:54.483 --> 02:55.999
Not at all.

02:56.001 --> 02:58.001
I'm high as a kite.

02:58.803 --> 03:00.354
If I'm looking forward
to anything,

03:00.356 --> 03:03.507
it's for that second
muscle relaxer to kick in.

03:03.509 --> 03:06.443
I hear you. Unfortunately,
I can't do that with my mom.

03:06.445 --> 03:07.945
I have to stay alert.

03:07.947 --> 03:11.448
Dinner with her is like being
trapped in a box with a snake.

03:11.450 --> 03:13.617
(laughs)
My mom's more like a hamster.

03:13.619 --> 03:15.819
They seem cuddly,
but they eat their young.

03:15.821 --> 03:17.521
Can't wait to meet her.

03:17.523 --> 03:18.739
Oh, you'll love her.

03:18.741 --> 03:20.690
Everybody loves her.

03:20.692 --> 03:23.043
She's sweet, shy and charming.

03:23.045 --> 03:25.796
Unless you happened
to come out of her uterus,

03:25.798 --> 03:27.965
then you're part
of a balanced breakfast.

03:27.967 --> 03:29.216
That bad, huh?

03:29.218 --> 03:32.086
Yeah, and it's gotten worse
since my dad died.

03:32.088 --> 03:33.887
Oh, she must have loved him
very much.

03:33.889 --> 03:35.339
Nah, hated his guts.

03:35.341 --> 03:37.091
She tried to kill him once.

03:37.093 --> 03:38.175
You're kidding.

03:38.177 --> 03:39.376
Yeah, they were playing golf.

03:39.378 --> 03:40.511
He gave her a swing tip.

03:40.513 --> 03:42.479
She hit him on the head
with a pitching wedge.

03:42.481 --> 03:44.064
A-a pitching wedge?

03:44.066 --> 03:45.549
It was the right club.

03:45.551 --> 03:47.401
They were about 90 yards out.

03:48.570 --> 03:50.821
Anyway, when he finally died
years later,

03:50.823 --> 03:53.073
she decided
he was the love of her life,

03:53.075 --> 03:54.324
moved into
a retirement community,

03:54.326 --> 03:56.660
and put a "gone fishing sign"
on her hoo-ha.

03:56.662 --> 04:01.198
Okay, guess I shouldn't
mention golf during dinner.

04:01.200 --> 04:02.833
Mm.

04:02.835 --> 04:04.368
Or fishing.

04:04.370 --> 04:07.421
Yeah. You might also want
to stay away from politics,

04:07.423 --> 04:09.506
religion or &lt;i>The Price Is Right.&lt;/i>

04:09.508 --> 04:10.507
&lt;i>The Price Is Right?&lt;/i>

04:10.509 --> 04:11.508
She misses Bob Barker.

04:11.510 --> 04:12.709
Hates Drew Carey.

04:12.711 --> 04:14.077
Oh, really?

04:14.079 --> 04:15.879
I think he's a wonderful breath
of fresh air.

04:15.881 --> 04:17.514
Do not say that.

04:19.300 --> 04:21.718
♪ Men.

04:21.720 --> 04:22.919
See, he's right
behind you!

04:22.921 --> 04:24.555
Ah!
He's right behind you!

04:24.557 --> 04:25.689
Move! Move! Duck!

04:25.691 --> 04:29.092
Ah, ah, don't worry, Junior.
I got this!

04:29.094 --> 04:31.111
Aah, crap.

04:31.113 --> 04:32.896
Watch and learn.

04:32.898 --> 04:35.532
Man, I used to be a lot better
at this.

04:35.534 --> 04:37.534
I guess
I'm just out of practice.

04:37.536 --> 04:39.286
That's 'cause
you got a girlfriend now.

04:39.288 --> 04:41.271
Yeah. Your thumbs
have gotten weak.

04:42.790 --> 04:44.625
That's why
I choose to be a bachelor.

04:44.627 --> 04:46.059
Yeah, that's why.

04:49.047 --> 04:50.780
So, what's the deal
with you and Zoey?

04:50.782 --> 04:51.915
Are you gonna marry her?

04:51.917 --> 04:54.284
I don't know.
I mean, I love her and all,

04:54.286 --> 04:56.220
but I just got out
of a marriage.

04:56.222 --> 04:58.388
Do I really want
to be back in one?

04:58.390 --> 04:59.806
Hell, yeah.
She's hot.

04:59.808 --> 05:01.391
It's not about how hot she is.

05:01.393 --> 05:03.477
Oh, thank you, Jake.

05:03.479 --> 05:05.913
It's about whether
she &lt;i>stays&lt;/i> hot.

05:09.851 --> 05:12.352
I mean, plus, there's some
serious stuff to consider.

05:12.354 --> 05:15.322
She has a daughter,
so I'd be a stepdad.

05:15.324 --> 05:17.407
My stepdad's a pretty cool guy.

05:17.409 --> 05:19.576
I mean, he's always
slipping me money.

05:19.578 --> 05:21.912
I think he feels bad
about replacing my dad.

05:21.914 --> 05:24.448
Or about banging
your mom.

05:24.450 --> 05:25.666
Shut up!

05:25.668 --> 05:28.285
Mm, doesn't feel
so good, does it?

05:28.287 --> 05:30.537
That's what
your mom said.

05:32.207 --> 05:35.292
All right, can we please talk
about something other than sex?

05:35.294 --> 05:37.711
Yes.
Okay.

05:37.713 --> 05:40.097
But for the record,
I'm not a virgin.

05:40.099 --> 05:42.049
Good to know.

05:42.051 --> 05:44.301
Neither am I.

05:44.303 --> 05:47.037
At least I think I'm not.

05:47.039 --> 05:48.705
It was dark.

05:48.707 --> 05:50.190
Could have been just leg.

05:52.277 --> 05:53.694
But that still counts.

05:53.696 --> 05:55.178
No, it doesn't.

05:55.180 --> 05:56.313
Right?

05:56.315 --> 05:57.864
Listen, if he thinks
he got laid,

05:57.866 --> 05:59.066
what difference does it make?

05:59.068 --> 06:01.952
Thank you.

06:01.954 --> 06:03.487
♪ Men.

06:03.489 --> 06:04.821
Mom, this is Alan.

06:04.823 --> 06:06.240
Alan, this is my mom Jean.

06:06.242 --> 06:07.541
Hi. Nice to
meet you.

06:07.543 --> 06:08.742
How are you?

06:08.744 --> 06:10.127
Uh, good, good.

06:10.129 --> 06:12.195
Although I-I got to admit,
I'm-I'm a little nervous.

06:12.197 --> 06:14.331
You know, I hope Mom likes me,
you know?

06:14.333 --> 06:15.749
Relax, Alan.

06:15.751 --> 06:17.000
When it comes to men,

06:17.002 --> 06:19.703
Lyndsey has never
set the bar very high.

06:19.705 --> 06:21.838
What's that supposed to mean?

06:21.840 --> 06:24.040
I'm just saying that
you've always gone

06:24.042 --> 06:26.042
for quantity
over quality.

06:26.044 --> 06:27.644
It's a choice.
I'm not judging.

06:27.646 --> 06:28.812
(sighs)
Oh.

06:28.814 --> 06:31.265
Come on, muscle relaxers.

06:31.267 --> 06:34.685
So, Alan,
do you have children?

06:34.687 --> 06:36.820
Uh, I do. I have a son.
Mm.

06:36.822 --> 06:38.105
That's good,

06:38.107 --> 06:40.774
'cause even if Lyndsey
could bear another child,

06:40.776 --> 06:44.060
I'm not sure
that would be the smartest move.

06:44.062 --> 06:45.895
Mom!

06:45.897 --> 06:47.197
Tell the truth.

06:47.199 --> 06:49.082
Do you want another one
like Eldridge?

06:49.084 --> 06:51.535
Let's just change
the subject.

06:51.537 --> 06:54.504
Does &lt;i>anybody&lt;/i> want
another Eldridge?

06:56.174 --> 06:58.175
How are things
at Sunset Village?

06:58.177 --> 07:00.377
Same old, same old.

07:00.379 --> 07:02.629
Well, actually, some
of the same old died,

07:02.631 --> 07:04.214
so we got some new old.

07:04.216 --> 07:06.216
Oh, th's awful.

07:06.218 --> 07:07.718
Not really.

07:07.720 --> 07:10.220
If you get to their condo
before the relatives,

07:10.222 --> 07:12.422
you can score
some great stuff.

07:12.424 --> 07:14.725
Oh, Mom,
you're not saying...

07:14.727 --> 07:17.110
How do you think
I got this lovely sweater?

07:17.112 --> 07:19.090
It certainly wasn't
a Mother's Day gift.

07:19.115 --> 07:20.315
(scoffs)

07:20.532 --> 07:22.149
(laughs)
Well, uh,

07:22.151 --> 07:25.402
if it comes up,
I'm a 40 regular.

07:25.404 --> 07:26.787
(laughs)

07:29.040 --> 07:32.709
So, Mom, do you want to do
anything special this weekend?

07:32.711 --> 07:35.162
I'll be happy doing
whatever you want.

07:35.164 --> 07:37.614
Oh, well, I-I thought maybe
tomorrow we could have lunch

07:37.616 --> 07:40.884
at the Santa Monica Pier,
then go for a walk on the beach.

07:40.886 --> 07:43.086
Oh, okay.

07:43.921 --> 07:45.889
We don't have to.

07:45.891 --> 07:47.424
No, that's fine.

07:47.426 --> 07:50.060
I'm not afraid of
homeless people.

07:51.429 --> 07:53.980
You know, your
daughter's a good lady.

07:53.982 --> 07:56.183
You did a great
job with her, Jean.

07:56.185 --> 07:57.734
Thanks.

07:57.736 --> 07:59.903
But it was touch and go
for a while.

08:01.272 --> 08:03.907
She told you about her
show business career, right?

08:03.909 --> 08:05.826
Seriously, Mom? Really?

08:05.828 --> 08:08.278
What? It was a
very nice movie--

08:08.280 --> 08:10.497
if you like pornography.

08:10.499 --> 08:14.317
Okay, I-I saw it, and-and
it wasn't pornography.

08:14.319 --> 08:16.870
Well, it wasn't &lt;i>Mary Poppins.&lt;/i>

08:21.008 --> 08:22.793
So,

08:22.795 --> 08:24.378
you guys graduate this year,
right?

08:24.380 --> 08:25.512
I do.

08:25.514 --> 08:26.630
I do, too.

08:26.632 --> 08:28.298
Well, that's what
you said last year.

08:28.300 --> 08:31.952
Yeah, but now, they're one
more year sicker of me.

08:33.170 --> 08:35.305
So what are you gonna do now?

08:35.307 --> 08:38.358
Well, we were hoping
we could work for you.

08:41.362 --> 08:42.863
Doing what?

08:43.698 --> 08:46.983
We'd be, like, consultants.

08:46.985 --> 08:50.704
And what would you
be consulting about?

08:50.706 --> 08:52.873
Well, that would be
our first consultation.

08:56.294 --> 08:57.627
How about this?

08:57.629 --> 08:59.996
We could tell you
what kids these days are into

08:59.998 --> 09:02.349
and then develop killer apps
to target that geographic.

09:04.135 --> 09:06.169
Demographic.

09:06.171 --> 09:07.587
No, Republican kids, too.

09:07.589 --> 09:09.556
Mm.

09:12.477 --> 09:15.061
All right, Consultants,

09:15.063 --> 09:17.380
tell me some of your app ideas.

09:17.382 --> 09:19.516
Okay, well, you know, uh,

09:19.518 --> 09:23.236
when you take a picture of
your junk and send it to a girl?

09:24.906 --> 09:27.207
Um... no.

09:28.225 --> 09:29.826
But I understand the concept.

09:29.828 --> 09:34.080
Okay, okay, well, this app
makes your junk look bigger.

09:34.082 --> 09:36.850
And you can customize it.

09:38.286 --> 09:40.120
You can customize your junk?

09:40.122 --> 09:42.238
Yeah, you know,
like silly hats,

09:42.240 --> 09:44.240
glasses, little messages.

09:44.242 --> 09:47.227
"Wish you were here."

09:48.095 --> 09:50.180
Get it? Get it?

09:50.182 --> 09:51.932
Yeah, I get it.

09:51.934 --> 09:55.101
So, it's like Photoshop,
but for your junk.

09:55.103 --> 09:58.472
We call it Junkshop.

09:59.307 --> 10:00.724
It's a good name.

10:00.726 --> 10:03.360
What do you do
if you already got big junk?

10:03.362 --> 10:05.645
Oh, way ahead of you.
Tell him about Boobshop.

10:05.647 --> 10:08.448
All right, you know
how girls always complain

10:08.450 --> 10:10.784
about one boob being bigger
than the other?

10:15.740 --> 10:18.408
Oh, thank God,
she's asleep.

10:18.410 --> 10:20.327
I don't think
I can last four days.

10:20.329 --> 10:22.445
Every word out of her mouth
pushes my buttons.

10:22.447 --> 10:24.464
Yeah, I saw.
She's like a ninja mom.

10:24.466 --> 10:26.383
She sneaks in,
destroys your will to live,

10:26.385 --> 10:28.117
and then,
disappears without a trace.

10:28.119 --> 10:29.285
So I'm not crazy?

10:29.287 --> 10:30.504
Oh, no, not at all.
Oh.

10:30.506 --> 10:32.672
In fact, it kind of makes me
grateful for my mom.

10:32.674 --> 10:33.473
What do you mean?

10:33.475 --> 10:34.791
Well, there's no sneaking

10:34.793 --> 10:35.976
and stabbing in the back.

10:35.978 --> 10:37.143
She just walks right up to you,

10:37.145 --> 10:38.678
and hits you in the face
with a lead pipe.

10:38.680 --> 10:39.896
(laughs)

10:39.898 --> 10:41.130
I wonder what would happen

10:41.132 --> 10:43.299
if we put them
in the same room together.

10:43.301 --> 10:44.651
Uh. Momageddon.

10:44.653 --> 10:46.135
(laughing)

10:46.137 --> 10:49.472
Although... it wouldn't be
the worst idea in the world.

10:49.474 --> 10:50.306
What?!

10:50.308 --> 10:51.575
Well, think about it.

10:51.577 --> 10:53.410
They're around the same age,
they're single,

10:53.412 --> 10:56.196
they're both deeply disappointed
in their children

10:56.198 --> 10:59.115
and their children's children.

10:59.117 --> 11:00.450
They might hit it off.

11:00.452 --> 11:03.820
And if they did,
it might give us a break.

11:03.822 --> 11:05.005
You know what? Tell you what--

11:05.007 --> 11:07.457
I will call my mom
and try to set up a dinner.

11:07.459 --> 11:08.625
Oh, Alan,

11:08.627 --> 11:10.326
that would
be wonderful. Mm.

11:10.328 --> 11:11.928
I owe you one.

11:11.930 --> 11:14.514
You still owe me one
from my birthday.

11:14.516 --> 11:16.633
(sighs) Well...

11:16.635 --> 11:18.852
if she wasn't here,
I'd be steering this car

11:18.854 --> 11:21.170
with the back
of my head right now.

11:24.308 --> 11:26.309
Looks like she's
sleeping pretty good.

11:28.946 --> 11:30.947
Oh, what the hell?
Scoot your seat back.

11:31.782 --> 11:34.534
ALAN:
&lt;i>Yay!&lt;/i>

11:45.106 --> 11:46.756
♪ Men.

11:47.591 --> 11:48.825
Hey, what you doing?

11:48.827 --> 11:50.093
Absolutely nothing.

11:50.095 --> 11:51.461
I'm bored out of my mind.

11:51.463 --> 11:53.463
Oh, well, Lyndsey and I
are having dinner with our moms.

11:53.465 --> 11:54.514
You're welcome to join us.

11:54.516 --> 11:56.449
A two-mom dinner?

11:56.451 --> 11:57.434
You can say no.

11:57.436 --> 11:59.135
No. God, no.

11:59.137 --> 12:00.503
I get you.

12:00.505 --> 12:01.888
I don't want to go, either.

12:01.890 --> 12:03.356
Why are you
doing it?

12:04.191 --> 12:05.725
Are you thinking
about getting married?

12:05.727 --> 12:08.111
Um, to answer your questions
in reverse order:

12:08.113 --> 12:10.063
not at the moment and oral sex.

12:10.065 --> 12:11.281
Night.

12:13.951 --> 12:17.320
Oral sex.

12:17.322 --> 12:19.522
Time to warm up the old milk.

12:20.708 --> 12:21.958
Oh, great, Amy.

12:21.960 --> 12:23.543
We'll be there.

12:23.545 --> 12:24.661
What's going on?

12:24.663 --> 12:25.745
Just got invited

12:25.747 --> 12:27.664
to a slammin' party
in the Valley.

12:27.666 --> 12:28.698
Cool.

12:28.700 --> 12:30.700
Can we borrow your car?

12:33.337 --> 12:35.755
Uh, all right, let me think.

12:35.757 --> 12:39.809
Two potheads want to borrow
my $100,000 car

12:39.811 --> 12:42.545
to go to a slammin' party
in the Valley.

12:43.397 --> 12:44.647
Sounds like a no.

12:44.649 --> 12:45.849
Wait, wait, wait.

12:45.851 --> 12:47.183
Let's hear him out.

12:47.185 --> 12:49.352
It's a no!

12:50.688 --> 12:52.489
I'll give you guys a ride.

12:52.491 --> 12:54.107
- Oh, sweet.
- Thanks.

12:54.109 --> 12:55.658
What you got going on
with the water?

12:55.660 --> 12:58.028
Oh, we had another idea
for an app.

12:58.030 --> 13:00.663
Let me guess-- Sinkshop.

13:00.665 --> 13:01.948
Oh, no, no.

13:01.950 --> 13:04.217
Okay, imagine the app
is on my phone.

13:04.219 --> 13:05.585
- All right.
- Go ahead.

13:05.587 --> 13:06.669
(inhales deeply)

13:06.671 --> 13:08.588
JAKE:
Now, all I do

13:08.590 --> 13:11.074
is press this button,
and our app will tell you

13:11.076 --> 13:14.361
exactly how long you can
hold your breath underwater.

13:19.717 --> 13:21.084
That's clever.

13:21.086 --> 13:22.268
Thanks.

13:22.270 --> 13:24.087
How is it different
than the stopwatch

13:24.089 --> 13:25.305
that's already
on your phone?

13:25.307 --> 13:26.756
The what?

13:26.758 --> 13:29.359
See this
little clock?

13:30.478 --> 13:32.278
Oh.

13:32.280 --> 13:34.764
Damn.

13:34.766 --> 13:37.050
How long?

13:40.871 --> 13:42.205
So this is nice, huh?

13:42.207 --> 13:43.289
Lovely.

13:43.291 --> 13:44.774
I can't remember
how long it's been

13:44.776 --> 13:46.776
since the last time
you called me to have dinner.

13:46.778 --> 13:48.411
Oh, come on. It hasn't
been that long.

13:48.413 --> 13:51.280
Oh, please.
Jake was still cute.

13:51.282 --> 13:53.616
Guess it has been awhile.

13:53.618 --> 13:54.968
So what's up with this dinner?

13:54.970 --> 13:57.387
Why are you finally allowing me
to meet your girlfriend?

13:57.389 --> 13:58.888
First of all, I wasn't
disallowing you

13:58.890 --> 14:00.456
from meeting her;
I was just, uh...

14:00.458 --> 14:02.759
avoiding it as long as possible.

14:04.128 --> 14:06.129
Uh, but things
are more serious between us now,

14:06.131 --> 14:07.514
and I thought it might be nice

14:07.516 --> 14:09.432
for you two
to get to know each other.

14:09.434 --> 14:11.968
- All right.
- And her mother might come along.

14:11.970 --> 14:13.019
Her mother?

14:13.021 --> 14:14.604
Yeah, she's, uh,
in town visiting.

14:14.606 --> 14:16.773
I thought you two
might hit it off.

14:16.775 --> 14:21.027
Alan, you know
I don't like old people.

14:22.196 --> 14:23.997
I do know, but you'll like her.

14:23.999 --> 14:25.648
She's young at heart,
like you.

14:25.650 --> 14:28.651
I'm young everywhere--
all the parts.

14:28.653 --> 14:29.819
Sure.

14:29.821 --> 14:30.920
What I haven't replaced,

14:30.922 --> 14:33.590
I've had tightened,
bleached or trimmed.

14:33.592 --> 14:35.508
Got it.

14:35.510 --> 14:37.326
So where's
the old biddy live?

14:37.328 --> 14:38.661
Palmdale.

14:38.663 --> 14:41.681
Palmdale, ech.

14:41.683 --> 14:42.999
Is she married?

14:43.001 --> 14:44.167
Uh, widow.

14:44.169 --> 14:45.185
How'd her husband die?

14:45.187 --> 14:46.352
Heart attack.

14:46.354 --> 14:47.604
Boring.

14:48.889 --> 14:51.357
She did actually try
to kill him once.

14:51.359 --> 14:52.475
Oh.

14:52.477 --> 14:54.260
Well, at least we have
something in common.

14:57.615 --> 14:59.616
Sure you gave me
the right address?

14:59.618 --> 15:00.950
Yeah.

15:00.952 --> 15:03.486
1478 Amy Lane.

15:03.488 --> 15:05.488
Wait a sec.

15:05.490 --> 15:09.125
Isn't Amy Lane the name
of the chick having the party?

15:11.495 --> 15:14.981
It may not be Amy Lane.

15:17.134 --> 15:21.087
But we're on
Amy Lane.

15:21.089 --> 15:23.840
An amazing coincidence, huh?

15:25.059 --> 15:27.177
Is there somebody
you guys can call?

15:27.179 --> 15:28.878
I mean,
I can call Amy Lane.

15:28.880 --> 15:32.182
If that is, in fact,
her real name.

15:33.150 --> 15:34.684
(thud)

15:37.188 --> 15:40.389
Evelyn, Alan tells me
you do a lot of traveling.

15:40.391 --> 15:42.025
Yes. I love it.

15:42.027 --> 15:44.827
The classical architecture,
the exotic cuisine,

15:44.829 --> 15:46.395
the uncircumcised men.

15:46.397 --> 15:48.198
(gags)

15:48.200 --> 15:50.116
Although one could make a case

15:50.118 --> 15:52.401
that falls under
"exotic cuisine."

15:52.403 --> 15:56.589
(whispering): Just like you and
Alan in the car.

16:01.629 --> 16:03.263
Do you guys travel much?

16:03.265 --> 16:04.747
Not anymore.

16:04.749 --> 16:07.884
But when my husband was alive,
we went everywhere.

16:07.886 --> 16:11.521
Six Flags, Epcot, Dollywood.

16:11.523 --> 16:12.922
Charming.

16:12.924 --> 16:14.857
Real globe-trotter.
(chuckles)

16:14.859 --> 16:17.927
Speaking of which, I once slept
with Meadowlark Lemon.

16:19.280 --> 16:20.980
Let me tell you,

16:20.982 --> 16:24.117
basketballs weren't
the only thing he could spin.

16:26.620 --> 16:28.771
(whispering):
I'm so sorry.

16:29.957 --> 16:31.241
I hope this is it.

16:31.243 --> 16:32.992
They have a balloon
on the mailbox

16:32.994 --> 16:34.777
that says party.
Mm.

16:34.779 --> 16:36.796
(doorbell rings)

16:37.948 --> 16:40.199
Yeah?

16:40.968 --> 16:43.286
Uh, is this
where the party is?

16:43.288 --> 16:46.122
Oh, you saw the balloon, huh?

16:46.124 --> 16:47.757
Come on in.

16:47.759 --> 16:49.309
Okay.
Oh, hang on.

16:49.311 --> 16:51.010
Hang on. Excuse us.

16:51.012 --> 16:53.563
Don't you pay attention
in health class?

16:53.565 --> 16:54.931
What are you
talking about?

16:54.933 --> 16:56.749
Stranger danger.

16:59.186 --> 17:01.237
No, he seems okay.

17:01.239 --> 17:03.639
You guys like to wrestle?

17:03.641 --> 17:05.441
Let's book it, dude.

17:05.443 --> 17:07.760
Yeah. Walden!
Don't go!

17:09.813 --> 17:12.148
Always a bridesmaid.

17:20.591 --> 17:22.125
Really, Alan?

17:24.762 --> 17:26.279
Why don't I get this?

17:27.715 --> 17:29.849
Well, you got to admit
my plan worked.

17:29.851 --> 17:32.302
They hit it off and left us
pretty much unscathed.

17:32.304 --> 17:34.837
Plus, thanks to your mom,
my mom can now go back

17:34.839 --> 17:37.023
to her retirement community
and show all her girlfriends

17:37.025 --> 17:39.359
what happens
when you Google "Santorum."

17:39.361 --> 17:41.477
(both laughing)

17:41.479 --> 17:44.530
Lyndsey, will you take me
to get a tramp stamp?

17:44.532 --> 17:45.948
What?

17:45.950 --> 17:48.568
It's a cute little tattoo
right here.

17:48.570 --> 17:49.852
Evelyn has one.

17:49.854 --> 17:51.070
You do?

17:51.072 --> 17:52.622
I got it in Singapore.

17:52.624 --> 17:55.792
The Chinese characters for:
"Thank you. Come again."

17:57.294 --> 17:59.829
All right, well,
we're done here.

17:59.831 --> 18:00.997
Why don't we head home?

18:00.999 --> 18:02.665
I don't want
to go home.

18:02.667 --> 18:04.700
Evelyn says there's a place
right down the street

18:04.702 --> 18:06.803
where they have music
and dancing.

18:06.805 --> 18:08.554
Oh, I don't think so.
It's getting kind of late.

18:08.556 --> 18:10.423
Yeah, we both have
to work in the morning.

18:10.425 --> 18:11.424
I don't.

18:11.426 --> 18:12.875
Neither do I.

18:12.877 --> 18:14.594
Why don't you two fuddy-duddies
run along

18:14.596 --> 18:16.879
and let Jean and I
have some fun?

18:16.881 --> 18:18.598
How will you get home?

18:18.600 --> 18:21.067
Alan, I made it from Brunei
to Morocco with nothing

18:21.069 --> 18:23.886
but the clothes on my back
and a tube of lubricant.

18:23.888 --> 18:27.407
I think I can get us
from Tarzana to Sherman Oaks.

18:27.409 --> 18:29.742
(giggling):
Isn't she a hoot?

18:29.744 --> 18:32.445
All right,
if you're sure.

18:32.447 --> 18:33.913
Let's go.

18:34.998 --> 18:37.417
You think we'll find
some cute fellas to dance with?

18:37.419 --> 18:39.369
Oh, Jean, Jean, Jean.

18:39.371 --> 18:41.621
We're not going
to dance.

18:44.541 --> 18:46.209
♪ Men.

18:46.211 --> 18:48.544
Should have written
the address down, dude.

18:48.546 --> 18:49.629
I did write it down.

18:49.631 --> 18:51.247
She must have told it
to me wrong.

18:51.249 --> 18:52.682
Or maybe you
heard it wrong.

18:52.684 --> 18:56.886
If only there was an app that
could capture the spoken word.

18:56.888 --> 18:58.521
(button clicks)

18:58.523 --> 19:02.525
(on phone): If only there was an app that
could capture the spoken word.

19:03.861 --> 19:05.445
Don't mock us, man.

19:05.447 --> 19:06.312
(button clicks)

19:06.314 --> 19:09.282
Don't mock us, man.

19:10.600 --> 19:12.785
Hi, Jake.

19:13.320 --> 19:14.237
Hi, Eldridge.

19:14.239 --> 19:15.872
- Hey.
- Hi.

19:16.773 --> 19:18.624
I bet they were
at the party.

19:18.626 --> 19:21.444
Yeah, maybe they can
tell us where it is.

19:21.446 --> 19:22.412
Oh, good thinking.

19:22.414 --> 19:23.830
I'll text 'em.

19:25.615 --> 19:27.616
Wait, I don't have
their numbers.

19:28.469 --> 19:32.088
Man, we're never going
to find this party.

19:32.890 --> 19:35.391
Okay.

19:36.643 --> 19:38.895
Let me ask you a question.

19:38.897 --> 19:42.398
If you had made it to the party,
what would you have done there?

19:42.400 --> 19:44.967
Try to hook up
with some chicks.

19:53.560 --> 19:55.745
Why don't you hook up with them?

19:57.247 --> 20:00.416
Right there--
that's why you're rich.

20:02.169 --> 20:05.671
Would you mind very much if
we, you know, blew you off?

20:05.673 --> 20:07.790
I would worry about
you if you didn't.

20:07.792 --> 20:09.876
- Bye.
- Later.

20:10.711 --> 20:12.428
ELDRIDGE:
Hello, ladies.

20:12.430 --> 20:14.630
JAKE: Mind if we
hook up with you?

20:23.502 --> 20:25.503
♪ Men.

20:25.505 --> 20:26.754
Morning.
Morning.

20:26.756 --> 20:27.838
Oh, morning.

20:27.840 --> 20:29.206
You and Evelyn have a
good time last night?

20:29.208 --> 20:30.991
Fantastic.
Mm.

20:30.993 --> 20:32.677
I adore your mother.

20:32.679 --> 20:35.012
(chuckling): That's only because
you just met her.

20:35.014 --> 20:38.349
I don't know, I think I got
to know her pretty well.

20:38.351 --> 20:40.918
Good morning,
darling.

20:42.604 --> 20:44.188
Hi, Peaches.

20:49.728 --> 20:52.513
Once again,
I'm so, so sorry.

20:52.515 --> 20:56.515
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color="#00FF00">elderman&lt;/font> ==

00:00.500 --> 00:02.000
